getarian cuisine|Vegetarian cuisine]] | [[Cookbook:Dessert|Dessert]]\n==Ingredients==\n\n* ½ [[Cookbook:Cup|cup]] [[Cookbook:Vegetable Oil|vegetable oil]]\n* ¼ cup white granulated [[Cookbook:Sugar|sugar]]\n* ¼ cup [[Cookbook:Brown Sugar|brown sugar]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Molasses|molasses]]\n* 1 [[Cookbook:Egg|egg]]\n* 3 cups [[Cookbook:All-purpose flour|all-purpose flour]]\n* 1½ [[Cookbook:Teaspoon|tsp]] [[Cookbook:Baking Soda|baking soda]]\n* 1 tsp ground [[Cookbook:Cinnamon|cinnamon]]\n* 1 tsp ground [[Cookbook:Ginger|ginger]]\n* ½ tsp [[Cookbook:Salt|salt]]\n* 1 cup [[Cookbook:Water|water]]\n\n==Procedure==\n\n# Preheat [[Cookbook:Oven|oven]] to [[Cookbook:Oven_temperatures|350°F]].\n# In a mixing bowl, [[Cookbook:Beat|beat]] the oil and the sugars.\n# Beat in molasses and egg.\n# Combine the flour, baking soda, cinnamon, ginger, and salt.\n# Stir into molasses alternating with water.\n# Fill greased or paper-lined [[Cookbook:Pots and Pans|muffin cups]] ⅔ full.\n# [[Cookbook:Bake|Bake]] for 20–25 minutes, or until a wooden toothpick comes out clean.\n# Cool in pan for 10 minutes before turning out to a [[Cookbook:Cooling Rack|wire rack]].\n\n[[Category:Inexpensive recipes]]\n[[Category:Dessert recipes]]\n[[Category:Baking recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes for muffins]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground cinnamon]]\n[[Category:Recipes using molasses]]\n[[Category:Vegetarian recipes]]\n[[Category:Holiday recipes]]\n[[Category:Recipes using baking soda]]\n[[Category:Recipes using brown sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using granulated sugar]]\n[[Category:Recipes using egg]]\n[[Category:Recipes using all-purpose flour]]\n[[Category:Recipes using ground ginger]]\n[[Category:Recipes using vegetable oil]]","isRecipe":true,"recipe":{"name":"Snappy Ginger Muffins","nameAr":null,"servings":null,"servingsSourceText":null,"ingredients":[{"id":"source-line-1","name":"½ cup vegetable oil","sourceText":"½ cup vegetable oil","amountText":"½ cup vegetable oil","amount":null,"unit":null,"fo